+**Keep the forest save on top.** The game's Load list is newest first, and every default run loads
+`KokiriForest_Child`. After a session that saved somewhere else, load the forest save and save again at once, so it
+does not sink down the list (asked for by the owner on 2026-11-17; done that night at 22:36, slot_02). A spec with `"resave": true` does it
+right after the load: Plus (pause menu), R (System tab, Save is its first entry), A (Save dialog, Cancel selected),
+Up, A (saves over the slot that was loaded), B. The run fails if the slot's `caption.sav` did not change. Leaving
+an area autosaves into slot_00, which also pushes the forest save down. `"hold_file": PATH` keeps the game open
+right after the load for manual debug-server calls until that file is removed.
+
 Rules the harness follows, from what went wrong: game state comes from memory, never from screenshots; `main`'s
 address is read from each boot's log (ASLR); never queue specs as separate waiters on "no queue.sh running" (they
 match their own command lines); a debugger attaches only once the guest is held.
